  "nl_text": "The database named rschema_0498 contains five tables, each with its own unique purpose. The first table, student_table, stores information about students, including their name, gender, age, dormitory, and class. The student_id column is the primary key, and the dormitory_id and class_id columns are foreign keys that reference the dormitory_table and class_table, respectively. The class_table contains information about classes, including the class teacher, number of students, and location. The class_id column is the primary key. The sports_team_table contains information about sports teams, including the team name, activity time, coach, activity venue, team ID, and affiliated school. The team_id column is the primary key, and the affiliated_school column is a foreign key that references the school_table. The school_table contains information about schools, including the school name and ID. The school_id column is the primary key. The dormitory_table contains information about dormitories, including the building number, administrator, and dormitory capacity. The dormitory_id column is the primary key.",
  "gold_question": "System Description\nDescribes a school management system\n\nMain functions of the system\n1: Student management: including basic information of students (such as student ID, name, gender, age) and accommodation information (such as dormitory number, building number, number of people, administrator)\n2: Class management: including basic information of classes (such as class number) and classroom information\n3: Sports team management: including basic information of sports teams (such as team name, activity time, coach, activity venue)\n4: School management: including basic information of schools (such as school name) and information of sports teams",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0498.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0498\nCREATE TABLE `student_table` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `dormitory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`dormitory_id`) REFERENCES `dormitory_table` (`dormitory_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_table_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `class_table` (`class_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `class_table` (\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_teacher` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_students` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`class_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sports_team_table` (\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_time` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `coach` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_venue` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `affiliated_school` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sports_team_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`affiliated_school`) REFERENCES `school_table` (`school_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `school_table` (\n  `school_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `school_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`school_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dormitory_table` (\n  `dormitory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `building_number` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `administrator` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `dormitory_capacity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`dormitory_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
